                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        {/* CHAPTER 07 — a HAZARD guarantee, and the second and last coloured
            ground on the page.

            Same test as 03, the other side of it. The claim is again the absence
            of an event — "an agent can't screw up" — and again unshowable: the
            console beside it demonstrates what an agent CAN reach, never that it
            failed to do damage. Coral because this promise is about a named
            danger not landing, and coral is the page's alarm hue.

            Dark ink, not white. Coral only exists as a colour at high lightness,
            so this is the one section on the site that inverts: white on #FB5066
            is 3.26:1 and fails AA, near-black is 6.11:1.

            The divider that used to introduce this chapter is gone. A coloured
            ground is a stronger version of the same gesture, and running both
            would have two devices doing one job. */}
        <div>
            <section class="chapter ground-raised relative border-y border-white/8 py-24 sm:py-32">
                <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center">
                        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
